abstract: |
  tidy-gmail is an open-source, local-first Python command-line
  utility for inspecting and cleaning Gmail accounts using
  user-maintained configuration and explicit cleanup rules.

  The project separates mailbox inspection, classification,
  cleanup decisions, and execution. It is designed to preserve
  personal correspondence, financial records, charitable
  contribution receipts, and other potentially valuable messages
  while identifying disposable email.

  Configuration, credentials, audit records, and reports remain
  under the user's control. The intended interface supports
  inspection, dry-run evaluation, controlled movement to Gmail
  Trash, and restoration.

